t":"industry_expert","point":"Saturday pop-up crowds may be a one-time draw. Weekday commuters and seated regulars pay the rent."}],"conditions":["The landlord agrees in writing to a permit-deadline termination right, with no four-month exit fee if the occupancy permit is not issued by a date you and your attorney set beyond the 6-8 week estimate.","Your attorney confirms the allowance letter binds a successor owner and that the 12-month exit clock runs from rent start, not signing. Both are unresolved.","You set a weekday sales walk-away number before looking at the weekday data, and Route 1 clears it.","Prince George's County confirms the plan review timeline and whether one certified food service manager can cover both sites or each site needs its own on duty (F10, F11, unverified).","Your accountant adds insurance, utilities, extra equipment and lender conditions to the cash model, and savings still stay at or above your $78,000 floor."],"next_steps":[{"when":"this week","action":"Ask the landlord for a permit-deadline termination right in writing, and for two or three weekday pop-up days in the space. If you cannot get those, ask for one to two more weeks on the two-week deadline."},{"when":"this week","action":"Have your attorney review the amendment. Ask whether the allowance letter binds a successor owner and when the 12-month exit clock starts."},{"when":"this week","action":"Call the Prince George's County Health Department environmental health program. Confirm the plan review timeline for a former food space, whether the manager and second credential holder can cover two sites, and what changes they commonly require to hood, grease trap or electrical work."},{"when":"this week","action":"Write down your weekday walk-away number: the minimum weekday sales per day, by morning and afternoon, below which you do not sign. Then compare it with weekday pop-up results and your first store's Square weekday data."},{"when":"next 30 days","action":"Ask your bookkeeper or accountant to add insurance, utilities, extra equipment, hiring and opening payroll to the SBDC downside model. Ask the Maryland SBDC to re-run it with weaker weekday sales."},{"when":"next 90 days","action":"After signing, file the plan review right away. Plan how the manager's time is split during the opening. Track how many Route 1 customers already buy at the first store, using your Square directory."}],"ai_tools":[{"name":"ChatGPT Plus","use":"Turn your Square sales exports into a rough weekday and daypart forecast to compare with the Route 1 pop-up data.","monthly_cost":"$0-20/mo","works_with":"Standalone; you upload Square sales exports by hand.","caveat":"It can produce confident numbers from weak inputs, and a first-store forecast does not prove Route 1 demand. Have your bookkeeper check every figure.","url":"","price_fact":"","pilot_test":"Keep it only if its weekday forecast for the first store lands within 15% of actual weekday sales from the last four weeks, by the landlord deadline. Otherwise drop it and use a spreadsheet."}],"escalate_to":"attorney","escalation_reason":"Lease amendment language, whether the landlord letter binds a successor owner, and when the 12-month exit clock starts all need your attorney. The county must confirm permit and credential rules directly.","would_change":["Weekday pop-ups or Square data fall below your walk-away number, which would move this to wait or decline.","The landlord refuses any permit-deadline protection, or your attorney finds the allowance letter or exit clock weak.","The county says each site needs its own credential holder on duty, or requires changes beyond the landlord letter and fixed-price contract."],"no_new_tool":"Use Square's own sales reports and a free spreadsheet to build the weekday and daypart forecast by hand, with your bookkeeper checking it. Cost: $0 plus a few hours."}},"artifactDelta":{},"requestedAuthConfigs":{},"requestedToolConfirmations":{}},"output":{"decision":"proceed","headl